# Two pipelines side by side: each is a group (a lane); links make the stages, so stages line up.
title "Two ways to read an image"
schema graph
mark img box input label="image"
mark px  box dense label="784 pixels"
mark hid box dense label="hidden layer"
mark out box output label="scores"
link f1 arrow img -> px label="flatten"
link d1 arrow px -> hid label="fixed W₁" color=blue
link d2 arrow hid -> out label="fixed W₂" color=blue
group mlp part-of=[px,hid] label="dense net"
Say: "A dense net |flat|flattens the image and multiplies by the same weights every time."
@flat indicate d1
mark p1 box token label="patch 1"
mark p2 box token label="patch 2"
mark p3 box token label="patch 3"
link t1 arrow img -> p1 label="cut"
link a12 arrow p1 -> p2 label="0.73" color=orange
link a13 arrow p1 -> p3 label="0.20" color=orange
link m2 arrow p2 -> out
group vit part-of=[p1,p2,p3] label="transformer"
Say: "A transformer cuts it into |cut|patches, and each patch weighs the others."
@cut indicate t1
mark key card text="Dense: fixed mixing. Transformer: mixing chosen by the data." label="Key idea"
Say: "Fixed mixing, against mixing the data chooses."
